From: somestupidgirl <sunnevanattsol@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kext_tools: mkextunpack's plist error no longer hides its flag

In the mkext2 entry loop, `CFErrorRef error' is declared to receive
CFPropertyListCreateWithData()'s failure, and shadows the function's own
`Boolean error'.  The three `error = true; goto finish;' lines after it
-- meant for that flag -- assign `true' to the CFErrorRef instead, so
finish: never sees the failure and returns the half-built entries array
rather than releasing it.  Modern clang refuses the int-to-pointer
assignment outright.  The CFErrorRef becomes plistError.

--- a/mkextunpack_main.c	2026-09-15 00:17:32
+++ b/mkextunpack_main.c	2026-09-15 00:17:32
@@ -789,15 +789,15 @@
             continue;
         }
 
-        CFErrorRef  error;
+        CFErrorRef  plistError;
         kextPlist = CFPropertyListCreateWithData(kCFAllocatorDefault,
                                                  kextPlistDataObject,
                                                  kCFPropertyListImmutable,
                                                  NULL,
-                                                 &error);
+                                                 &plistError);
         if (!kextPlist) {
-            errorString = CFErrorCopyDescription(error);
-            CFRelease(error);
+            errorString = CFErrorCopyDescription(plistError);
+            CFRelease(plistError);
             if (errorString) {
                 CFIndex bufsize = CFStringGetMaximumSizeForEncoding(
                 CFStringGetLength(errorString), kCFStringEncodingUTF8);
